&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a globally distributed engineering team, creating an environment where team members can do their best work and grow their careers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, onboard, and develop engineers, setting clear expectations for quality and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product management and cross-functional engineering teams to shape the roadmap, make sound architectural decisions, and deliver against product commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set expectations for reliable, secure, maintainable, and performant delivery, and help the team meet them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage the use of artificial intelligence as a core part of how the team works, with engineers using artificial intelligence tools in their daily workflows to improve efficiency and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold regular 1:1s, provide continuous feedback, and support engineers&#39; professional growth through coaching and skill development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track milestone progress, identify blockers early, and address patterns before they require escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the incident management on-call rotation to help maintain availability targets for GitLab.com.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing engineering team, including advising on architecture and contributing to technical discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed systems and durable workflow execution, including state persistence and replay patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or managing teams working on release orchestration, deployment automation, or continuous delivery at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Kubernetes deployment patterns and GitOps workflows, including progressive delivery strategies such as blue/green and canary deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with policy-based governance and event-driven architectures in reliable, enterprise-grade delivery systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and managing teams in early-stage contexts, including defining processes, hiring foundational team members, and establishing how the team works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across functions, exercising judgment, and moving work forward in ambiguous or fast-changing situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience communicating clearly in writing and conversation while working effectively in a remote-first, asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Engineering Manager, Continuous Deployment role is part of GitLab&#39;s broader DevOps engineering organization, working on software delivery experiences that help customers ship with assurance. We solve complex deployment challenges in a way that fits GitLab&#39;s single-platform approach, with close coordination across product, engineering, and infrastructure. This work brings together platform architecture, delivery reliability, and GitLab&#39;s evolving artificial intelligence strategy in a highly visible product area. We work in an all-remote, handbook-first environment and practice transparency, teamwork, and iteration. We focus on creating technology that helps organizations manage deployments more safely and effectively while contributing to GitLab&#39;s mission to enable everyone to contribute to and co-create the software that powers our world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab&#39;s APJ Ecosystem team builds and scales the partner (channel, alliance, and hyperscaler) motion across the region. ASEAN is a strategic market for GitLab, and this hire is central to strengthening our partner ecosystem there — deepening a smaller number of high-value partnerships rather than spreading thin across many transactional ones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Singapore, our Ecosystem Sales Manager (ESM)- ASEAN, is a senior, market-facing role responsible for building and scaling GitLab&#39;s partner business in ASEAN countries across the full breadth of the ecosystem: hyperscalers, large ASEAN-centric system integrators (SIs), and born-in-the-cloud / AI-native partners. We are looking for someone with the range and seniority to credibly own strategic partner relationships across all of these partner types, and to help grow our business through these partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual-contributor role for someone who has already built a career scaling partner-sourced and influenced revenue in ASEAN, someone who knows the hyperscaler ecosystem (AWS &amp;amp; GCP), has deep, credible relationships with ASEAN&#39;s major SIs, and understands how to engage newer-generation cloud-native and AI partners as they become an increasingly important part of the go-to-market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale GitLab&#39;s partner-sourced and influence business in ASEAN across hyperscalers, large ASEAN-centric SIs, and born-in-the-cloud/AI partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep, strategic (not transactional) relationships with a focused set of priority partners — joint business plans, QBRs, and named executive sponsorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own hyperscaler relationship management and Marketplace motion with AWS and/OR GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and grow relationships with major ASEAN SIs and market-making channel/born-in-the-cloud partners and emerging AI-native partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive partner-sourced pipeline and bookings, and carry a quota tied to partner-sourced/generated revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the ASEAN sales team to ensure partner-sourced opportunities are properly identified, supported, and closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the ASEAN and APJ Ecosystem team to help shape and refine the ASEAN Ecosystem coverage model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to partner enablement, certification, and go-to-market programs suited to the ASEAN market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on partner engagement health, pipeline contribution, and progress against strategic-partner milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in channel/alliance/partner management or ecosystem sales, ideally within enterprise software, DevOps, or cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive, well-rounded experience scaling a business through partners across hyperscalers, large ASEAN-centric SIs, and born-in-the-cloud/AI-native partners — not narrowly specialized in just one partner type.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience managing hyperscaler relationships (AWS &amp;amp; GCP) including Marketplace motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong, credible existing network among ASEAN&#39;s major SIs and cloud-native/channel partners, with a track record of moving relationships from transactional to strategic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort carrying a partner-sourced revenue quota and being measured on pipeline origination, not just deal closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills — able to align internal sales, marketing, and partner-side stakeholders around joint goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at or with a hyperscaler (AWS, GCP) in a partner or alliance capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GitLab, DevSecOps, or adjacent developer-tooling ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping design or reset a partner coverage model, comfortable building process rather than only inheriting one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like (First 6–12 Months)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Joint business plans and an active engagement cadence (e.g., QBRs) in place across priority hyperscaler, SI, and cloud-native/AI partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable movement of key partner relationships from transactional to strategic engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing partner-sourced pipeline and bookings against quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible input into finalizing the ASEAN Ecosystem coverage model, grounded in on-the-ground partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
